# Build context, shared by BOTH Dockerfiles in this repo.
#
# ONE FILE, BECAUSE THERE CAN ONLY BE ONE. Per-Dockerfile ignore files
# (Dockerfile.blackwell.dockerignore) are a BuildKit feature, and this machine's
# docker has BuildKit enabled but no buildx component, so builds run on the
# classic builder -- which reads `.dockerignore` and nothing else. Two ignore
# files that only one builder reads is exactly the kind of silently-inert
# configuration this project keeps paying for.
#
# `Dockerfile` (CUDA 11.8) is toolchain-only and COPYs nothing, so the context
# is irrelevant to it beyond a few seconds of tar. `Dockerfile.blackwell`
# (CUDA 12.8) COPIES THE WHOLE REPO IN -- that is the point of it: the tag pins
# a commit and a rented machine runs `docker run` with no clone and no build.
#
# So what is excluded here is exactly the artifact trees -- ~120 GB of past runs
# and archives, none of which is an INPUT to anything the image does. A seed is
# a flat uniform spin-up: empty topoFile, empty inFile, no sounding, no terrain,
# no land cover. data/grid* is carried anyway (4 MB) because the same image also
# runs corpus cases, which do read it.
.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# --- artifact trees ---------------------------------------------------------
runs
figures
pairs
pairs_npz
pairs_npz_retired
jobs24

# jobs/ IS THE RETIRED 16 m LIBRARY AND ONLY ITS TWO SCRIPTS ARE NEEDED.
# jobs/run_seed.sh and jobs/seed_watch.sh drive production; the eighteen 16 m job
# DIRECTORIES under it are not read by anything the image runs (bin/run_seeds.py defaults
# --jobs-dir to jobs30).
#
# AND EXCLUDING THEM BY ARTIFACT PATTERN DID NOT WORK, MEASURED: `jobs/*/FE_*` is a
# ONE-LEVEL pattern -- `*` does not cross `/` -- and four of those directories keep their
# dumps one level deeper, in `jobs/<seed>/smoke_aside/FE_SMOKE.{0,20520}`. Eight files at
# 73,271,565 bytes: **560 MB inside the image**, on a layer DEPLOY.md tells the operator to
# push to a registry, against an intended payload of ~59 MB. The Dockerfile assertion meant
# to catch exactly this globbed only /flux/jobs30/*/ and passed.
jobs/seed_*
jobs30/*/output
jobs30/*/return
jobs30/*/window
jobs30/*/FE_*
jobs30/*/*.log

# --- data: the small model grids stay, the archives go ----------------------
data/raw
data/hrrr
data/smokelib
data/case_grids

# --- results: the JSON/txt record stays, the arrays go ----------------------
results/**/*.npz
results/**/*.nc

# --- the FastEddy fork's own artifacts and non-inputs -----------------------
FastEddy-model-5.0.1/.git
FastEddy-model-5.0.1/**/*.o
FastEddy-model-5.0.1/SRC/FEMAIN/FastEddy
FastEddy-model-5.0.1/tutorials
FastEddy-model-5.0.1/docs

# --- prebuilt binaries: the image compiles its own --------------------------
lib/liblpdm.so
